{#-
  Shared front-matter values.

  The Norwegian knowledge model describes a single research project per DMP
  (chapter "About the research project"), so there is no plural/singular choice to
  make as there was with the list-based dsw:root model.
-#}
{%- set project = replies.researchProjectChapter -%}
{%- set admin = replies.administrativeInformation -%}
{%- set projectName = project.name._value if project and project.name else "" -%}
{%- set dmpTitle = admin.dmpTitle._value if admin and admin.dmpTitle else "" -%}

{#-
  Integration replies (ORCID, ROR, ...) are markdown, so the "markdown" filter wraps
  them in <p>. Dropping that wrapper keeps a value usable in an inline run - a list
  item or a table cell - where a block-level paragraph would otherwise split the line
  and leave an empty paragraph behind. The round-trip through "string" is needed
  because "replace" on a Markup value escapes its arguments.

  Use this only for single-paragraph values; multi-paragraph ones (the local policy
  integrations, with their bullet lists) belong in a block, see the "md" class.
-#}
{%- macro mdInline(text) -%}
  {{- ((text|markdown)|string|replace("<p>", "")|replace("</p>", ""))|safe -}}
{%- endmacro -%}
